{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Honor your father.</b> I have already mentioned that in the first five commandments HaShem is mentioned, and the name is joined with all of them: \"YHWH your Elohim\"." "<b>And the word 'they shall be prolonged.'</b> A verb in the construct state, for they will be the cause, and the witness is \"and that your days may be prolonged\" (Deuteronomy 11:9) and \"you will prolong days\" (ibid. 22:7). On account of the commandment that you perform, it turns out that you prolong your days." "And he said \"upon the land,\" for when Israel keeps this commandment they will not be exiled from it. And it is written: \"Father and mother they have trifled with you\" (Ezekiel 22:7). Now, in the commandment of honoring father, one must not do the opposite, to curse or to treat lightly [מקלה], and one is liable to death for cursing, for the hearers hear the curse from his mouth; but one is not liable thus for מקלה, for מקלה can also be done in secret. Therefore Scripture decreed that it be with the word ארור, like all the passages that are in secret."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Resolved הַשֵם as HaShem per voice rules for reverent forms.", 2 "Kept מקלה untranslated throughout, as Ibn Ezra appears to use it as a technical term for humiliating or degrading a parent; the precise sense and derivation are uncertain. The antecedent of צוה הכתוב (whether it refers to the Decaluge or to Leviticus 20:9 / Deut. 27:16) is left ambiguous as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:17.149126491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}